HEAD \u003cfile\u003e...\" to unstage)\n\n\tnew file:   123.txt\n\tnew file:   125.txt\n````","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493970020,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5OTQwMTk5NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1413#issuecomment-299401995"},"message":"So the issue is our logic for detecting whether we need to call `save` at the end of `add`. Two possibilities: 1) we improve this to also scan the staged content and make a more valid decision, or 2) we don't care and always call `save`.\n\nI will go for 2, because we have other issues with this kind of situation in `save` (e.g. #1419) and we better make them all end up in the same piece of code and solve it in there -- properly, if possible.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493970456,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5OTQwMzEyMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1413#issuecomment-299403123"},"message":"Disabling detection brings us here:\n\n````\nmih@meiner /tmp/addtest (git)-[master] % datalad add *\nadd(notneeded): /tmp/addtest/123.txt (file) [/tmp/addtest/123.txt is already included in the dataset]\nadd(notneeded): /tmp/addtest/125.txt (file) [/tmp/addtest/125.txt is already included in the dataset]\nsave(ok): /tmp/addtest (dataset)\nAction summary:\n  add (notneeded: 2)\n  save (ok: 1)\nmih@meiner /tmp/addtest (git)-[master] % git st\nOn branch master\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\nmih@meiner /tmp/addtest (git)-[master] % git reset HEAD~1\nmih@meiner /tmp/addtest (git)-[master] % git add .\nmih@meiner /tmp/addtest (git)-[master] % datalad add .\nadd(notneeded): /tmp/addtest (directory) [nothing to add from /tmp/addtest]\nsave(ok): /tmp/addtest (dataset)\nAction summary:\n  add (notneeded: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n````\n\nPartial `add` seems to work fine too:\n\n````\nmih@meiner /tmp/addtest (git)-[master] % git st\nOn branch master\nChanges to be committed:\n  (use \"git reset HEAD \u003cfile\u003e...\" to unstage)\n\n\tnew file:   123.txt\n\tnew file:   125.txt\n\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add \u003cfile\u003e...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\n\t678.txt\n\nmih@meiner /tmp/addtest (git)-[master] % datalad add 123.txt 125.txt\nadd(notneeded): /tmp/addtest/123.txt (file) [/tmp/addtest/123.txt is already included in the dataset]\nadd(notneeded): /tmp/addtest/125.txt (file) [/tmp/addtest/125.txt is already included in the dataset]\nsave(ok): /tmp/addtest (dataset)\nAction summary:\n  add (notneeded: 2)\n  save (ok: 1)\nmih@meiner /tmp/addtest (git)-[master] % git st\nOn branch master\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add \u003cfile\u003e...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\n\t678.txt\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present (use \"git add\" to track)\n````\n\nWill now look into the implications of this change.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493971077,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEwNzAxNjU4NjU="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1494157380,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTA3MTg0ODE1MA=="},"status":2}]}